From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:57:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733: Let the GPU0 clock set the rate of
 PLL_GPU0

GPU0 divides PLL_GPU0 by 1, 2, 4, 8 or 16, but passes no rate request
to its parent. A consumer of GPU0 can therefore only pick a divider of
whatever rate PLL_GPU0 has, 840 MHz out of reset, and the board has to
set PLL_GPU0 itself, with assigned-clock-rates on its own clock.

Set CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT, so that a rate request on GPU0 reaches
PLL_GPU0, and CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT. GPU0 can also take
PLL_PERIPH0 and its taps, which feed other consumers: without the flag
the rate search tries every parent and may re-rate PLL_PERIPH0. With it
the search stays on the parent the board selected.

PLL_GPU0 has CLK_SET_RATE_GATE, so the request fails with -EBUSY while
the PLL is prepared; nothing changes for a rate set before the GPU
enables its clocks.

The board's assigned-clock-rates already set PLL_GPU0 to 1008 MHz before
GPU0, so the request for 1008 MHz on GPU0 finds the parent at that rate
and changes nothing for it.

Not covered: the rate request of the GPU driver, which the next patches
add.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: on two boards the GPU driver's rate request
on GPU0 set PLL_GPU0 to that rate with GPU0 undivided while the PLL
output was gated, and the GPU firmware booted.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
index 33ccf88ad8f5..78b0579a82b7 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -925,7 +925,9 @@ static struct ccu_div gpu0_clk = {
 		.reg		= 0xb20,
 		.features	= CCU_FEATURE_UPDATE_BIT,
 		.hw.init	= CLK_HW_INIT_PARENTS_DATA("gpu0", gpu_parents,
-							   &ccu_div_ops, 0),
+							   &ccu_div_ops,
+							   CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT |
+							   CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT),
 	}
 };
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(bus_gpu0_clk, "bus-gpu0", ahb_hws, 0xb24, BIT(0), 0);
